From 9abed8c957f2c1a6cd551de950af426034e02d8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:56:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] daemon, app: resend chatbot responses as they went; fetch
 failed pictures again

A suggestion response is kept as it went: the response JSON (as before)
and now the imdn.Message-ID it answers (a new inReplyTo column). Resend
on a failed one (the long-press menu) sends exactly that again through
SendSuggestionResponse (resendSuggestionResponse on the daemon), never as
text and never as SMS or MMS; when the bot cannot be reached it stays
failed. A suggested action's response is stored too, so that it can go
again, but the conversation lists it only while it is failed (RCC.07 shows
nothing for an action); a failed one that comes after the bot's next
message goes in its place by time.

In a chatbot's conversation (by SIP URI, or a number a bot wrote from)
nothing RCS was chosen for becomes SMS or MMS: a refused or failed text,
a refused file and a failed upload are failed messages, to be sent again.
What the conversation would send as SMS anyway (no chat capability, R9
7.7.3.1) still goes as SMS.

A picture that did not come (card media, thumbnails, open rich card
images, bot icons) shows "Image failed to load, tap to retry", and is
fetched again on demand only: when it is shown again (at most every 30 s,
and not after 3 failures in a row), always when tapped, and once when the
network comes back (QNetworkInformation reachability, from Qt Network;
without a backend, the other two). Nothing runs in between.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L5scTQJJDo2PTt6GBeDFah
